dialect protocol
protocol stdio.png.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.png.op
start op

# Real binary op-frame `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` NOW emit for `PngMutation` —
# upgraded, this program, from the F6-era `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (see this artifact's report). `tag u8` is the mutation's own ordinal (this enum cannot use
# `#[derive(dsl::DslOps)]` — `SetTransparency`/`SetBackground` carry genuine data-carrying enums
# directly, `SetSnapshot` transitively via `PngSnapshot`, see 🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs's own
# doc comment — so the ordinal is hand-assigned, declaration order: NoMutation=0,
# SetSnapshot=1, SetHeader=2, SetPalette=3, SetTransparency=4, SetGamma=5,
# SetChromaticities=6, SetSrgbIntent=7, SetPhysicalDims=8, SetTimestamp=9, SetBackground=10,
# InsertTextChunk=11, RemoveTextChunk=12, SetTextChunk=13, SetPixels=14,
# InsertUnknownChunk=15, RemoveUnknownChunk=16). Every genuinely scalar field below (the
# ordinal, `index`, and `SetHeader`'s five IHDR fields) is individually, honestly byte-walked
# and validated. Every OTHER field carries a nested, tri-state-or-enum-shaped payload
# (`Option<T>`/`Option<Option<T>>`/`PngTransparency`/`PngBackground`/`PngTextChunk`/`PngChunk`/
# a whole `PngSnapshot`) — one length-prefixed opaque `bytes` tail per arm, deliberately placed
# LAST so it can honestly consume exactly its own declared span with no further length prefix
# needed at the protocol-description level. `Prim::Ref` to a struct/enum still unconditionally
# errors at walk time (confirmed unchanged since P2-M2) so these nested shapes aren't further
# protocol-walkable field-by-field — the Rust `encode_op`/`decode_op` implementation IS
# genuinely, fully structured real binary (see 🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs's
# `RealBinaryOpFrame` region), this is purely a limit on how deep the PROTOCOL DESCRIPTION
# itself can validate structurally (same documented limitation as every other stdio pilot's
# own nested-payload arm, e.g. csv's `snapshot bytes`/`record bytes`).
framing record
repeat op {
tag u8
arm 0 { }
arm 1 { snapshot bytes }
arm 2 { width u32 height u32 bit_depth u8 color_type u8 interlace u8 }
arm 3 { plte bytes }
arm 4 { trns bytes }
arm 5 { gama bytes }
arm 6 { chrm bytes }
arm 7 { srgb bytes }
arm 8 { phys bytes }
arm 9 { time bytes }
arm 10 { bkgd bytes }
arm 11 { index varint chunk bytes }
arm 12 { index varint }
arm 13 { index varint chunk bytes }
arm 14 { pixels bytes }
arm 15 { index varint chunk bytes }
arm 16 { index varint }
}
